<title>USA: Global Med unit gets contract.</title>
<headline>Global Med unit gets contract.</headline>
<dateline>LAKEWOOD, Colo. 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global Med Technologies Inc said that its Wyndgate division has signed a 10-year contract to provide blood bank management software to Haemonetics Corp.</p>
<p>The company said it was a &quot;multimillion-dollar&quot; contract, but did not provide a specific value.</p>
<p>Haemonetics intends to provide Wyndgate's SAFETRACE software for use in blood banks, Global Med said. Haemonetics provides blood separation products to blood banks and hospitals.</p>
</text>
